# Thesis 05: Service SKUs is much more important than the file makes it look

The current file is tiny: standardized qualification fields, certifications, duration, parts, ranges, exclusions, warranties and evidence.

But this is arguably **the Rosetta Stone of the entire service business**.

Today:

```text
"electrician"
"EV installer"
"plumber"
```

are useless categories for an autonomous agent.

An agent needs:

```text
EV-INSTALL-7KW-STANDARD
postcode: NG7
off_street_parking: true
supply: single_phase
cable_run_m: 8
charger: zappi_v2
fuseboard_upgrade: false
certification_required: OZEV
expected_duration: 2.5h
price_band: £800–£950
```

Now Jim, Sarah and ABC Electrical aren't merely “electricians.”

They are **fulfillment nodes for particular service SKUs**.

That is huge.

And importantly, UCP is now creating a common commerce capability language rather than requiring every agent to learn every merchant backend. Drop should therefore be designed as a **service-domain superset/extension of these emerging standards**, not another entirely separate ontology. ([Google Developers Blog][1])

